The paragraph states that benchmark contamination is a critical concern. It then describes prior works that have quantified contamination using various matching strategies (n-gram/token overlap, longest substring, skipgram, full-text exact). It mentions Sainz et al. (2024) for data contamination from multiple sources. Then it says that indexing large-scale pretraining corpora is expensive and prior studies are limited in scale (up to RedPajama-1T and Dolma). Finally, it claims that their work is the first to do contamination analysis on the largest open corpora.

